  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "PERCENTRANK.EXC truncates to significance decimal places (not significant digits) and returns 1 for singletons",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, PERCENTRANK.EXC(array, x, [significance]) computes the exclusive rank (i + 1)/(n + 1) with linear interpolation and truncates the result to significance decimal places (trunc(value * 10^places) / 10^places, default 3) rather than significance significant digits. When array holds a single numeric entry matching x, Excel returns 1 before checking significance <= 0. In compatibility version 1, @PERCENTRANK.EXC returns #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 49 PERCENTRANK.EXC rows in dcj9k_statistics and prefix_metadata (row 177) in Excel 16.0.20527.20088, and matched across 2,864/2,864 full-bank PERCENTRANK.EXC rows.",
